    "help": {
      "format": "restructuredtext",
      "content": "\n\n========\nSynopsis\n========\n\nRenames collection element identifiers using a mapping from a file.\n\n===========\nDescription\n===========\n\nThis tool changes the element identifiers (names) in a collection without modifying the datasets themselves. The new identifiers are read from a file you provide.\n\nThree mapping modes are available:\n\n========\nExamples\n========\n\n**Simple text file — positional renaming**\n\nEach line in the text file replaces the identifier at the same position in the collection. Given a collection::\n\n List:  sampleA, sampleB, sampleC\n\nand a text file::\n\n Alpha\n Beta\n Gamma\n\nthe output is::\n\n List:  Alpha, Beta, Gamma\n\n.. class:: infomark\n\nThe text file must have exactly as many lines as the collection has elements (when **Ensure strict mapping** is enabled).\n\n-------\n\n**Two-column tabular file — lookup renaming**\n\nThe first column contains the current identifier, the second column the new one. Order does not matter::\n\n sampleB    Beta\n sampleC    Gamma\n sampleA    Alpha\n\nOutput::\n\n List:  Alpha, Beta, Gamma\n\n-------\n\n**Extended tabular — choose which columns to use**\n\nWorks like the two-column mode, but the file may have additional columns. You select which column holds the original identifiers and which holds the new ones.\n\n-------\n\n.. image:: ${static_path}/images/tools/collection_ops/relabel.svg\n  :alt: Relabel collection element identifiers from a file\n  :width: 500\n\n-------\n\n.. class:: warningmark\n\nValid identifiers must contain only letters (a-z, A-Z), numbers (0-9), dash (-), underscore (_), dot (.), space ( ) and comma (,). Other characters are not allowed.\n\n.. class:: infomark\n\nThis tool will create new history datasets copied from your input collections but your quota usage will not increase.\n\n    "
    }
  },
